			"author": {
				"name": "Alan",
				"url": "https://aus.social/@alansuspect",
				"avatarUrl": "https://avatars.webmention.io/cdn.masto.host/7eb948923c37a822e8df01ca6f5e455c5383713d09f4b03b03d9f02fa46fb40f.png"
			},
			"date": "2025-04-29T23:28:11.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> I was looking at your webshare web component: <a href=\"https://www.zachleat.com/web/webcare-webshare/\"><span>https://www.</span><span>zachleat.com/web/webcare-websh</span><span>are/</span></a> and it's awesome!</p><p>The thing it raised for me (and I guess the web share API in general) is how differently we use our devices. </p><p>On mobile this component is great because I can easily share through my apps, but on desktop (macos for me) I get a weird list of default apps I don't use (Mail, Notes, Freeform..?) and no way to share to something social media-ish. Also there's no share integration with a browser at all, which on desktop is where I do most of my interaction.</p><p>This is just a comment though, I have no idea if this is a fixable thing, or even needs fixing and is working correctly ????????‍♂️</p>\n<a href=\"https://www.zachleat.com/web/webcare-webshare/\">webcare-webshare Web Component—zachleat.com</a>",
			"type": "mention",
			"via": "webmention"
		}
	],
